/-- The elementary coefficient calculation behind a reciprocal-radius
interval.  Unlike the stationary-phase theorem, this is purely algebraic and
is valid also for the planar circle (`n = 1`). -/
theorem short_interval_l2_coefficient_le_frequency_decay_of_any_dimension
    {n : ℕ} (C0 C1 : ℝ) (hC0 : 0 ≤ C0) (hC1 : 0 ≤ C1)
